# Python Expiry Job Review Checklist

Use when reviewing `expiry-job/` changes.

## Architecture

- [ ] No MySQL/direct DB access — HTTP API only
- [ ] Snapshot-first fetch (no PATCH between GET pages)
- [ ] Matches `docs/process-flow.md` and Decision #11, #18, #20

## Correctness

- [ ] Uses `Asia/Colombo` date for evaluation (explicit `ZoneInfo`)
- [ ] Buffer from `COMPLIANCE_EXPIRING_BUFFER_DAYS`
- [ ] Sends PATCH only when computed status ≠ current
- [ ] Accepts downgrades (`expiring` → `active`) when applicable
- [ ] Event payload matches Decision #7 schema; `runId` unique per run

## Idempotency & reliability

- [ ] Skips when computed status already matches current `status`
- [ ] Retry/backoff + timeout on external calls
- [ ] Failed batches logged; job does not crash entire run
- [ ] Login once; re-login on 401 for that request only

## Security & config

- [ ] Credentials from env only
- [ ] HTTPS in non-local environments
- [ ] No hardcoded AWS account IDs or ARNs

## Tests

- [ ] Tests for transitions, boundaries, idempotent rerun, empty snapshot
- [ ] HTTP client mocked; no live AWS required in unit tests

## Output format

List issues by severity with file path and fix. State "no blockers found" if clean.
